# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own value.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way: DATABASE_URL is a write credential,
# and anyone holding it can overwrite or delete every NAV and file the dashboard
# serves.
#
# ONE VALUE NEEDS CHANGING: the Neon connection string.
# Neon console -> your project -> Connect -> copy the connection string
# (the pooled one is fine). It looks like:
#   postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#
# The pipeline creates its own tables on first use (schemes, nav_history,
# files), or run:  python scripts/neon_store.py --init
#
# The same value is read by the Vite dev server (site/vite.config.ts) to serve
# /data/* locally. For the deployed site, set DATABASE_URL in Netlify's
# environment variables; for the nightly job, as a GitHub Actions secret.

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://YOUR-USER:YOUR-PASSWORD@YOUR-ENDPOINT.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
